From 39fa02911d2c0ab6674d81aa518dfd8286d13faf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:48:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] ppc: add AltiVec rasterizer

All four tile functions for both tile sizes, generated from one template
header like the C version.  The C reference computes in int16_t
throughout, so the modular 16-bit vector operations are an exact
transcription; vec_packsu implements its final FFMIN(val, 255) clamp.
update_border_line needs a per-lane (x * w) >> 16, which is assembled
from vec_mule/vec_mulo and one permute picking the high halfwords.
---
 libass/ppc/rasterizer_altivec.c          |  37 +++
 libass/ppc/rasterizer_altivec_template.h | 277 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 314 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libass/ppc/rasterizer_altivec.c
 create mode 100644 libass/ppc/rasterizer_altivec_template.h

